# The host's settings for the deploy kit. Copy this file to ~/services/skyblock-collector/deploy.env
# and set the lines you need; each line left out keeps the default shown. Every script reads it
# when it runs. A new address or port reaches the pod only when install.sh or update.sh deploys,
# which renders the pod's unit and restarts the pod for it: run install.sh from the release's
# checkout, or update.sh --force, to apply it now. Until then verify.sh can't reach the status
# server, which it already looks for at the new address.

# The address the status server and Postgres (for the read-only `reader` login) listen on, such as
# the host's address on a private network. The default keeps both on this host only.
#BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
#STATUS_PORT=3004
#PG_PORT=5432

# The SSH host that runs the secondary collector on another internet connection, as `ssh` names it
# on this host, and its processor (arm64 or amd64). Empty runs no secondary collector.
#SECONDARY_HOST=
#SECONDARY_ARCH=arm64

# A podman auth file with read access to the image, read in place, for a private image only. Give
# an absolute path or one under $HOME. The image of this repository is public, so the default
# pulls without a credential.
#REGISTRY_AUTHFILE=

# 0 makes install.sh and update.sh leave the timers that deploy releases, make restore points and
# pull the secondary's files as they are, instead of enabling them.
#ENABLE_TIMERS=1
